   Amsterdam and Haarlem},
Journal = {COMUNICACION Y SOCIEDAD-GUADALAJARA},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {21},
Abstract = {This paper analyzes artificial lighting as a means of changing human
   perception. It presents oil lamps used in Haarlem for domestic lighting
   and in Amsterdam for urban lighting in the seventeenth century. The
   theoretical framework is media archaeology. The methodology used is
   qualitative archaeological, involving the analysis of different sources
   including texts, images, archival documents and archaeological remains.},
