   0.25), 0.98 (+/- 0.12), 0.45 (+/- 0.27), and 0.36 (+/- 0.11) were
   recorded during the autumn, winter, spring, and summer seasons,
   respectively. Furthermore, switching on ceiling fans and opening doors
   and windows improved occupants' thermal satisfaction during different
   seasons. The study results show the effective use of environmental
   controls and the role of thermal adaptation in enhancing the
   subjects/overall thermal satisfaction in the composite climate of India.},
